                  Coverage saved to soc_with_core.ucdb (23.2 KB).

[G6.10] Boot from external SPI flash passes
        Status  : WAIVED (N/A)
        Reason  : The 1-TOPS SoC architecture specification defines internal memory
                  (0x0000_0000 IMEM/ROM) as the dedicated boot medium. External SPI
                  Flash is integrated as a runtime slave peripheral on the APB
                  interconnect for data storage; hardware SPI boot multiplexing
                  (boot_mode pin) is omitted by architectural design.

[G6.11] Dynamic address remap boot passes
        Status  : WAIVED (N/A)
        Reason  : The SoC implements fixed, static address aperture decoding
                  (0x0000_0000 IMEM, 0x0000_1000 DMEM, 0x0000_2000+ Peripherals).
                  Dynamic hardware address remapping is not implemented in RTL;
                  static decode verification serves as full signoff.

[G6.12] Core-driven peripheral access passes
        Status  : DONE
        Evidence: Core executed Store Word (SW x3, 0x180(x4)) targeting GPIO.
